    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d575">

                <pb facs="0882" n="872" xml:id="pg872"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commander of the Seventh Fleet</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cooke</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to General Marshall
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-08-26">26 August 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>260520Z. Pursuant my 230318,<anchor n="46" xml:id="d575-f1"/> General Rockey is
                    conferring with CNA<anchor n="47" xml:id="d575-f2"/> Commander of 11th War Area
                    to arrange relief of Marines that will permit concentration at key points.
                    Prospects for quick success through Rockey’s efforts only are not bright. Any
                    assistance you can give by insisting on present CNA strength remaining along
                    railroad or by increasing CNA strength there will expedite relief of Marine
                    train guards and dispersed detachments. ComGen First Marine Div 250022<anchor
                        n="48" xml:id="d575-f3"/> passed to you refers.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
